you  I've already been introduced you know  about me you know that I'm an alumni two  children went here but there's a much  closer tie to hillsdale college than  just being alumni of Hillsdale and I  want to tell you a little story in the  next few minutes Larry mentioned if you  read the luncheon that there's a  monument over in front of central hall  just a few hundred yards from here and  it's for those hillsdale college  students which fought and what we now  call the Civil War or as my  mother-in-law's family calls it the war  of Yankee aggression but those hillsdale  college students paid the ultimate  sacrifice and if you haven't seen that  Monument I would encourage you to do  that because it's quite moving but they  paid their young lives for ideals and  morals that we still glorify here today  at the college and that is what this  school still stands for but I want to  tell you that at the time that those  young Patriots were giving their lives  there was a man who also fought for the  Union Army and he was engaged in that  conflict from Anderson Indiana his name  was Gideon Daniel Cyril now he was  wounded in battle but he was unimpressed  with the drugs that they used to treat  his wounds so he figured there might be  a business opportunity there so he  started to research those drugs used for  treating infection which led him  eventually to start a pharmaceutical  company and he named a GD searle &amp;  Company now the company grew into a  modest-sized chicago-based  pharmaceutical company that by the 1930s  was producing over a thousand individual  products but it was still a small  struggling company as the country went  into the Great Depression now mr.  Searles brand son by the name of John  Searle had graduated from the University  of Michigan School of Pharmacy we like  to joke around here  that's that school up the street there  and in 1936 mr. John Searle succeeded  his father dr. Howard Claude Cyril as  president of the company and he started  that company on a brand new course one  of his key decisions that he made after  becoming president 1936 of this small  struggling Midwest pharmaceutical  company that his grandfather GD had  started was to concentrate on medicines  that would represent therapeutic  breakthroughs now you remember at the  time the company was producing over a  thousand different products will he  greatly cut that down to narrow in on  just 30 products he focus on and  expanded research which finally  culminated in the introduction of  products that were original and that  made great contributions to the field of  medicine these new products eventually  helped the company become a major player  in the world wide pharmaceutical  industry among the better known of these  project products was a minnow fillin for  asthma Dramamine for motion sickness  probe an teen for peptic ulcers  Metamucil for constipation and  diverticulitis aldactone for  hypertension and edema lomotil for  diarrhea and in Ovid like it or not the  world's first birth control pill and  finally a spurt am known as nutrasweet  or by its market name of equal now mr.  Cyril built not only an excellent  organization but he selected and  developed outstanding men and women you  start to see the tie here between  Hillsdale mr. Cyril always believed in  the human capacity to accomplish great  things which is by the way why he hated  the progressive movement and the new  dealers because he believed their  philosophy and way of thinking stifled  creativity and the work ethic plus he  thought they were just a bunch of  thieves anyway and that they took  hard-working people's money  he was never content to merely keep pace  with the status quo but was determined  to maintain a leadership role for his  company he made the company's motto  research in the service of mankind and  that exemplified his goal in life now  his granddaughter my wife Louise and I  and the Searle family partnered with  this College because we see the same  commitment the same standards and  philosophy at this institution as the  surra family has sought to file for so  many years Hillsdale College has built  not only an excellent organization but  has selected some of the finest staff  and the finest faculty that can be found  we have gathered some of the finest  free-thinking young men and women to be  educated here several of them are here  in the audience today and I have the  pleasure of knowing some of them dr.  Arnn along with the trustees of this  school believe our country is in grave  danger at this moment in history as we  said earlier today we may even be on the  edge of despotism yet we are not  discouraged and we are standing up and  fighting because we believe that though  we are small in size these young people  that come here to learn some of whom  will graduate tomorrow will leave here  with the capacity and desire to  accomplish great things lord knows our  country and world needs them at this  very time we are not content to keep  pace with the standards of our nation  education system but we are also leaders  this school is doggedly persistent in  its goals and objectives just as the  sural company was that is why we invest  these material gains from the past into  this remarkably fiercely independent and  effective college we believe Hillsdale  College will impact our country and our  world in ways we have yet to see now  this building which is going to take  place behind us will have an entranceway  in a gathering place for hopefully what  will  be the very unique bright and persistent  hard working people to come together to  learn to listen to discuss to strategize  to create ideas and hopefully have a  huge significance and will even be  breaking bread together there and that  these same people will leave here with  ideas and motivations that may just  impact and transform our culture in our  world I invite you to please come back  and be part of that group finally I'd  like to thank the Lord God from whom all  gifts flow and I want to thank the  College for all it's meant to me in my  life I'm going to thank my fellow  trustees led by our chairman Bill  Broderick who loved this place and with  whom it is an honor to serve with I want  to thank also particularly John cervini  for starting this ball rolling and for  dr. Larry yarn for his great vision that  he's had for all this and I finally want  to thank the Searle family most  importantly my wife Louise for whom  without this gift you wouldn't be  possible thank you very much for this  opportunity of partnership and for being  here today

